Regression isolation rerun (2026-08-29, Asia/Shanghai)
- The formal VM repository had an uncommitted 119-line change in app/velawear_agent/drivers/velawear_pan.c. Its SHA-256 was 93f186a77f0c57b2c15efd97573aecad09879aee33b2e424cd9986a862575a0e.
- That change added Classic PAN visibility/name/class setup after BLE initialization. The corresponding image was 5,995,912 bytes with SHA-256 88736123a7191542e0b875d12e116dacbd76796df898a56133d1433bcd92f960. Two independent Windows scans found no VelaWear and matching_service=0; the BLE HIL stopped before CCCD enablement.
- For the A/B control, the formal branch version of velawear_pan.c was built in the same Ninja process. The build source SHA-256 was 0c3a202b066470834a46b88093f1ae957fbfe6bddab03d959b650593e1dc241d; the object contained no Classic PAN strings; nuttx.bin was 5,994,568 bytes with SHA-256 773d09a15be2cc469aefeed4037adf37250e29124a612af68809a62110718f16.
- The control image was flashed at 1,000,000 baud to 0x12010000 with verify. Cold boot returned BLE HCI status 0x00 for 0x2006, 0x2008, 0x2009, and 0x200a and printed advertising start ret=0.
- Windows then observed VelaWear at CDAB78563412 with RSSI -24 to -30 dBm, matching_service=7. The full HIL completed with service_status=0, all five characteristic statuses=0, cccd_status=0, threshold_before=100e, threshold_after=100e, and notifications=[000000].
- Conclusion: the BLE regression is reproduced and isolated to the uncommitted Classic PAN app change in combination with the current SiFli Bluetooth HCI adapter. The known-good control image remains on the board; the uncommitted change was not added to this submission PR.

Local Mock LLM BLE round trip (2026-08-29, Asia/Shanghai)
- Board image: known-good control image, nuttx.bin SHA-256 773d09a15be2cc469aefeed4037adf37250e29124a612af68809a62110718f16; no firmware changes were made for this test.
- Host bridge: Windows VelaWear LLM bridge connected to BLE identity CD:AB:78:56:34:12 and sent one CHAT_INPUT message: "今天有点累，陪我聊两句".
- Mock service: a loopback OpenAI-compatible HTTP endpoint returned "今天也要记得休息和喝水。" exactly once; the bridge reported bridge_exit=0.
- Mock request body used model mock-velawear and contained the board-originated prompt; this confirms the board request reached the host bridge and the response was written back over BLE.
- Concurrent 1 Mbps UART snapshot captured VelaWear boot, BLE advertising, and connected err=0x00.
- This is a local protocol/HIL proof only. It does not prove the contest-required team-maintained server, a real cloud LLM conversation, visible LCD rendering, physical touch, audible speaker output, voice wakeword, or the required demo video.



SHOW_REMINDER Agent command round trip (2026-08-29, Asia/Shanghai)
- Board image: known-good control image, nuttx.bin SHA-256 773d09a15be2cc469aefeed4037adf37250e29124a612af68809a62110718f16; no firmware changes were made for this test.
- The Windows BLE bridge connected to CD:AB:78:56:34:12 with trigger_reminder enabled and sent Agent command sequence 1, command id 3 (SHOW_REMINDER), argument 2 (REST).
- Concurrent 1 Mbps UART evidence: [BLE] Agent command queued: seq=1 id=3; [BLE] Agent command handled: seq=1 id=3 result=0.
- The board generated one LLM request for "AI 建议：休息一下"; the loopback OpenAI-compatible Mock endpoint returned "现在休息一下，喝口水吧。".
- Concurrent 1 Mbps UART evidence: [BLE] LLM response accepted: seq=1 status=0 bytes=36; [LLM] request=1 cloud_bridge connected=1; [Display] Companion phase=0 text_bytes=36; [Action] LLM response delivered.
- The bridge observed one completed Mock HTTP request and stopped after the response. This proves the Agent command, LLM request, BLE response, and software display-state transition path.
- The display-state log is not proof of human-visible LCD output; the loopback Mock is not the contest-required team-maintained server or a real cloud conversation. Physical display, audio, Skill tool execution, scheduled/proactive Skill behavior, and voice wakeword remain unverified.

Classic PAN visibility follow-up and source/image reconciliation (2026-08-29, Asia/Shanghai)
- Root-cause triage used the Windows WinRT classic Bluetooth selector from BluetoothDevice.get_device_selector() with DeviceInformation.create_watcher_aqs_filter(...), not the unfiltered device watcher.
- The filtered watcher enumerated three nearby classic devices, including the configured phone peer A4:C3:BE:A3:B5:3D, but no VelaWear, sifli_pan, or board identity. This proves the Windows classic inquiry path was active while the board was not observed.
- The earlier forwarding candidate removed only the Classic opcode cases from sf32lb52_bt_emulate_cmd. Candidate image size was 5,995,832 bytes and SHA-256 fb3614dcf2e3b60b5a879f9319842f12c287f5d645ce4d61292784b2c6cd4ac0. It was flashed with the standard 1,000,000-baud, 0x12010000, verify flow; BLE/GATT and local Mock LLM HIL passed, but the filtered classic scan still returned no board.
- The candidate was not adopted. The board was then rebuilt from the current VM worktree without the temporary vendor edit: app/velawear_agent/drivers/velawear_pan.c SHA-256 93f186a77f0c57b2c15efd97573aecad09879aee33b2e424cd9986a862575a0e and vendor/sifli/chips/sf32lb52/sf32lb52_bth4.c SHA-256 d7a57ef7108c8db5a236f452b65066f496ca9ceefef282213096c0423407979b.
- Current image: cmake_out/lckfb_huangshan_pi/nuttx.bin, 5,995,912 bytes, SHA-256 1efe61d627e1029c6d42a3f3a033563a208a2da68f8f8e431ab7d73a940d5465. Ninja completed 37/37 with warnings only. The image was flashed and verified at 1,000,000 baud to 0x12010000.
- Current cold boot: SFBL/ABCD; LCD /dev/lcd0 and touch /dev/input0 opened; BLE HCI 0x2006/0x2008/0x2009/0x200a returned 0x00; advertising and GATT registered; [PAN] Classic local name: sifli_pan; [PAN] Classic PANU visible; no sf32lb52 bth4 hardware-error line.
- Independent BLE regression on this current image passed with service_status=0, service_count=3, all five characteristic statuses=0, status_read=000000, cccd_status=0, and notifications=[000000].
- A second filtered classic scan on this current image again enumerated only the same three nearby classic devices (including A4:C3:BE:A3:B5:3D); board_match=[].
- Correction to the earlier regression-isolation paragraph: the later standalone BLE regression on the current PAN image passed. The earlier wrapper failure was a serial-open/scanner timing race, not proof that the PAN app change breaks BLE. The current finding is narrower: application PAN/HCI setup logs and BLE success do not establish classic RF visibility; the forwarding candidate also failed independent classic discovery. Classic controller/RF support remains unverified and no PAN end-to-end or real phone DHCP bridge is claimed.
- The board now matches the current VM worktree hashes above, but both PAN/vendor changes remain uncommitted local VM work and are not part of the submission PR unless separately reviewed.
